// Bars and shops (FacilityType). Copied into the world when a scenario starts. The park builds them anywhere on its land
// with a gravel path, platform, station or parking lot close by (facilityRules.accessReachMeters): paid at once
// (buildCostCents), open at once, then a daily upkeep (staff, stock). They serve the guests nearby
// (facilityRules.serveReachMeters): guests between laps, riders stopping on their way to a trail, guests going home.
// products: what it sells (data/products.json; one park-wide price per product, Finances menu).
// Bars (kind "bar"): `seats` guests can sit at a time (lunch, après-bike); impulse buys need no seat. Where a scenario has
// bars, guests only buy food at a bar: without a seat they ride on and try after the next lap; whoever finds none by the
// end of the lunch window eats a packed lunch (no money for the park, little mood).
// Bike shops (kind "bikeShop"): everything bike in one building, grown by its upgrades (each one a visible extension):
// shelfSlots departments the player picks from the unlocked ones (merch, clothing, protectors, parts, later bikes; Store
// tab), one range for the whole shop (budget / standard / premium, facilityRules.shopRanges: price, goods, upkeep and who
// buys), and `workbenches` in the workshop: bikes broken in a crash are fixed there (product "repair"), and the services
// the upgrades unlock (tune-up, suspension setup) take a bench too. The rental counter upgrade adds a fleet of bikes the
// park buys (bikeCostCents each, up to maxFleet), rented by the day (product "rental") to extra guests without a bike,
// mostly beginners (e-bike upgrade: anyone, and they pedal up cheaply); bikes wear per run and crash and are retired at 0 %,
// unless the workshop services the fleet each night (fleet care). `look` (upgrades): which extension the game draws.
// requiredLevel: the park level needed to build it.
